    "narrative": "The offense for Ghost Ride the WHIP hinges on top-of-the-order aggression and exploiting favorable matchups against struggling starters. **Brice Turang** earns today\u2019s highest efficiency score (67.64) by leading off against Rocker; the +10% order bonus combined with the favorable matchup profiles him as our primary engine for Runs and the scarce Stolen Base category. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** (66.80) and **Jose Caballero** (64.72) are locked into high-leverage spots, with **Mickey Moniak** benefiting from a robust +14% platoon edge against Mahle, and **Jose Caballero** leveraging a +13% platoon boost against the lefty Suarez to secure our mid-range production. **Josh Naylor** rounds out our elite tier at 76.43, as the combination of Scherzer\u2019s 5.40 xERA and the protection of the #5 spot makes him our most bankable asset for RBI production today.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Isaac Paredes**, who hovered near the 50-point mark but ultimately fell short due to a -9% platoon penalty against Thornton. While **Isaac Paredes** provides a solid floor, the optimizer prioritized the higher ceiling of **Austin Riley** (62.60) against Adams, where the +18% SP skill adjustment outvalued the relative stability of the bench options. We remain cautious of **Seiya Suzuki** (52.47); although he benefits from a +8% order bump, he faces a stiff test against Burns, whose talent suppresses his scoring potential despite the park factor. We have successfully avoided the sub-40 floor with **Zach McKinstry**, who is benched due to a brutal -19% SP skill penalty against Glasnow, ensuring we do not burn plate appearances on inefficient matchups that threaten our cumulative efficiency caps.",
